        "id": 17483,
        "name": "MattiasM",
        "username": "MattiasM",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/edb3f5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-05T13:48:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In the first scene of the first issue of the starter kit, the players are fighting a group of  mechanical spiders. The game suggests some twist examples, involving hindering or damaging heroes with a min die, or max for a major twist.</p>\n<p>The issue is that the environment doesn’t have any dice. Am I missing something, or was this an oversight? If I am missing something, what am I rolling? The starter guide has a thing about rolling d4s if nothing applies, but that seems to be geared towards hero overcome checks.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:50:33.073Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 4,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 20.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 17480,
        "topic_slug": "twist-dice-issues",
        "display_username": "MattiasM",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
